Kandor – patch 4: the AMDSupport fix as a Lilu patch (replaced the on-disk patch of earlier versions)
Apply after patches 1–3 (see README.md). Author: JessiesFlying, with assistance from Claude (Anthropic)
SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-only

Patches OCLP's Monterey AMDSupport 4.0.8 in memory when it loads (kernel 22+, krygpu=AMD), with the same five
find/replace pairs as the earlier on-disk patch (8 bytes, P3 matches twice). No system-volume change, no kmutil,
survives OCLP re-patching and macOS updates. Disable with -krynoagdc. On Apple's native AMDSupport or an already
patched one the patterns do not exist and nothing is changed.
Tested 21 Nov 2026 on Sonoma 14.8.9, Sequoia 15.8.1 and Tahoe 26.7.2 (Mac Pro 6,1, RX Vega 56).

